vercel:index/projectProtectionBypass:Pro.description:
Provides a Project Protection Bypass resource.

A Project Protection Bypass is an automation bypass token that allows automation services
to bypass Deployment Protection on a <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`vercel.Project`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`vercel.Project`" pulumi-lang-go="`Project`" pulumi-lang-python="`Project`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`vercel.Project`" pulumi-lang-java="`vercel.Project`">`vercel.Project`</span> using the `x-vercel-protection-bypass` HTTP header.

Multiple bypasses can be created per project. Exactly one bypass per project may have
<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`isEnvVar " pulumi-lang-dotnet="`IsEnvVar " pulumi-lang-go="`isEnvVar " pulumi-lang-python="`is_env_var " pulumi-lang-yaml="`isEnvVar " pulumi-lang-java="`isEnvVar ">`is_env_var </span>= true`; that bypass is exposed as the `VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET` environment variable on deployments.

